ue of $s+t?$\n\n$s+t=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297195 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c1e37e75-7d0c-5923-8a40-5f706dc21da1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297195 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $s$ and $t$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n(-s+3)x+2t=x+6\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n-s+3=1.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $s,$ we get\n\n$$\ns=2.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we have\n\n$$\n2t=6.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\nt=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $s=2$ and $t=3,$ we have\n\n$$\ns+t=2+3=5.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476103 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186110719.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186476103 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "393aec7c-08a3-58cd-ac4d-3705704af62b" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186476179 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476187 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186476179 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186476179 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(6p-6)x=36x\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186476179 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3c6ffd8f-aed0-5462-a678-623c3eb10c91" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186476179 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=6p-6,\\,b=36.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n6p-6=36.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6p & =42 \\