 case, \n\n$$\na=t+4,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\nt+4=2.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\nt=-2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549054 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186548879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549054 #edb/ref 1069 "q-288560" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549054 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549054 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(r-7)x=-x\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $r?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549054 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d6ec3c46-2316-5f98-be70-c232b5719be1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549054 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=r-7,\\,b=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\nr-7=-1.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\nr=6.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549090 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3b9efce2-cc34-5966-9ee7-777169e666e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549090 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186297195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549108 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186549129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549108 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "70e3dbbc-f265-58ec-abc4-fa61aa670f9a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549108 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186549054 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549129 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186549090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549129 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9c38efa4-70b9-572d-aabd-a33044024fc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549129 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186549009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549131 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186549108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549131 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a60530a2-2052-544d-a2a2-f6b827880aca" #